From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] color: a DCI-P3 red counts as wide gamut

BIsWideGamut() uses the red primary as its sentinel and takes a red y strictly
below 0.320 as the sign of a wide-gamut panel. DCI-P3 red is exactly
(0.680, 0.320), so a panel described with P3 primaries lands precisely on the
threshold and is classified narrow.

That is every one of our internal AMOLEDs: the display profile declares P3
primaries for the whole DDIC family. The effect is not that the SDR gamut
wideness slider goes dead -- both branches of buildSDRColorimetry() respond to
it -- but that it drives the wrong one:

  narrow branch (what we get)   source lerps PANEL NATIVE -> GENERIC WIDE GAMUT,
                                with a full blend-to-unit-cube saturation remap
  wide branch (what we want)    source lerps REC.709 -> PANEL NATIVE, no remap

So on a panel that genuinely has P3 to spend, the slider declares the content
WIDER than the display and then spends itself compressing the excess back in,
and the panel's own measured primaries are never an endpoint at all. At the
shipped default of 0.5 that is the worst of it: source = generic wide gamut plus
the full smooth remap, where it should be halfway between 709 and the panel with
no remap. Make the comparison inclusive, and pin the boundary with a test.

The one-character fix is virtudude's. The two-branch reading above and the
[color] test are ours.

diff --git a/src/color_helpers.cpp b/src/color_helpers.cpp

RE-ROLLED 2026-09-14: regenerated against a base without the 0008-0013 EDID/HDR series,
which was retired when HDR was dropped (issue #93). Nothing here changed in intent -- the only
difference is that hunks which used to carry HDR-introduced context (create_color_mgmt_luts's
bTraditionalHDROutput parameter, the DrmHdrOutputRequiresVulkanComposition call site, and test-list
entries for deleted tests) now sit on the pristine signatures instead. Generated with git diff, not
hand-edited.
---
diff --git a/src/color_helpers.cpp b/src/color_helpers.cpp
index 6459ef2..0aba314 100644
--- a/src/color_helpers.cpp
+++ b/src/color_helpers.cpp
@@ -925,8 +925,12 @@ std::optional<glm::vec3> calcScanoutLinearScale(
 
 bool BIsWideGamut( const displaycolorimetry_t & nativeDisplayOutput )
 {
-    // Use red as a sentinal for a wide-gamut display
-    return ( nativeDisplayOutput.primaries.r.x > 0.650f && nativeDisplayOutput.primaries.r.y < 0.320f );
+    // Use red as a sentinal for a wide-gamut display. The bound has to be inclusive:
+    // DCI-P3 red is exactly (0.680, 0.320), so every panel profiled with P3 primaries --
+    // which is how our internal AMOLEDs are described -- lands precisely on it and would
+    // otherwise be called narrow, leaving the SDR gamut wideness slider to clip instead of
+    // mapping between Rec.709 and the native gamut.
+    return ( nativeDisplayOutput.primaries.r.x > 0.650f && nativeDisplayOutput.primaries.r.y <= 0.320f );
 }
 
 void buildSDRColorimetry( displaycolorimetry_t * pColorimetry, colormapping_t *pMapping,
